tests/sun -- the sun-path gate
==============================

    make sun-verify TOOLCHAIN=sun
                                gmake on Solaris; tests/sun/run does the work

On Solaris, with Sun's toolchain (REQUIREMENTS.SOLARIS), it builds the MDs of
every config and the hypervisor of legion and checks:

    - the four MD blobs hash to tests/full/md/expected/blobs.sha256, the pins
      the gnu path is held to: both paths give the same bytes;
    - q.bin and reset.bin are built, q.bin has its version string and carries
      no build directory and no cc command line (Sun cc's debug stubs are
      removed before the link, patches/hv/hv-sun-strip-debug.patch);
    - the cases of tests/full/workdir and tests/full/guards (what the work
      directory and the Makefile guards do on Solaris, with gmake 3.82).

It needs only bash, strings, egrep and digest(1) besides the build's own
tools. It does not boot anything: there is no QEMU here. To boot a sun-built
set, take it to a Linux host and run tests/smoke/run <dir> or
tests/full/login/run <dir>.

Booting the sun-built sets:
    tests/sun/login-sets DIR...
    make sun-login-verify SETS="DIR..." GUEST_DISK=<image>
run the login gate of tests/full/login once per set, on a Linux host, and
print one line per set (`ok  NAME  login prompt ...` or `FAIL NAME ...`). A
DIR is a firmware set or a directory with the set in DIR/set; the set is named
after the DIR, so name the DIRs after the compilers that built them. Not part
of test-all.

On any other system it prints `skip` and exits 3 (make turns that into success
and tests/run-all shows SKIP). Env: OUTDIR (scratch; the logs md.log and
hv.log are kept there; `gmake sun-verify` gives it a directory inside WORKDIR,
and without one the test uses $TMPDIR and removes it when it passed), MAKE
(default gmake).
